==Battleground==
*1 [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 34.67~37.33 seconds<sup>1,040f~1,120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 46.67~49.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,480f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Rel]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*1 [[Dagshund]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>, delay 14.67~17.33 seconds<sup>440f~520f</sup>.
*1 [[Dagshund]] spawns after 116.67 seconds<sup>3,500f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 156.67 seconds<sup>4,700f</sup>, delay 14.67~17.33 seconds<sup>440f~520f</sup>.
*1 [[Dagshund]] spawns after 203.33 seconds<sup>6,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The rushers you packed for Queen V like [[Jelly Dumpling Cat]], [[Can Can Cat]], [[Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Courier Cat]] are equally applicable here. Just DPS down Papuu and you win. If you ran [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] for Queen V, you  win instantly. If you used [[Fried Chicken Cat]] for Queen V, you win even faster than instantly.

==Trivia==
*Saintly Sister's Japanese name, Saintly Elder Sister (聖おねえさん ''Seinto Oneesan''), is a reference to either the manga ''[[wikipedia:Saint Young Men|Saint Young Men]]'' (聖☆おにいさん ''Seinto☆Oniisan'') or "[https://youtu.be/GodqyOjwmtg Saint☆Ojisan]" (聖☆おじさん ''Seinto☆Ojisan''), the [[wikipedia:Denki Groove|Denki Groove]] and [[wikipedia:Scha Dara Parr|Scha Dara Purr]] song that inspired said manga. This is corroborated by [[Divine Daughter (Merciless)|Divine Daughter]]'s Japanese name (聖★おねえさん ''Seinto★Oneesan''), which is nearly identical to Saintly Sister's, but with the addition of a star between the two words.

